description:
What: Replace the current check_credentials() string-equality stub in dispatch.rs with the async CredentialStore.check() call.
Algorithm:
1. The current AUTHINFO PASS handling in dispatch.rs calls check_credentials() synchronously
2. Problem: dispatch() is sync, but bcrypt verify is CPU-bound and slow
3. Solution: Move AUTHINFO PASS handling outside dispatch into lifecycle.rs (same pattern as GROUP/OVER):
   if let Command::AuthinfoPass(ref password) = cmd {
       let user = match ctx.pending_auth_user.take() {
           Some(u) => u,
           None => { write 482; continue }
       };
       let ok = stores.credential_store.check(&user, password).await;
       if ok {
           ctx.state = SessionState::Active;
           ctx.authenticated_user = Some(user);
           write Response::authentication_accepted();
       } else {
           write Response::authentication_failed();
       }
       continue;
   }
   Similarly handle AuthinfoUser outside dispatch.
4. Update dispatch.rs to return 500 for AUTHINFO (since it is now handled outside)
   Or better: leave AUTHINFO USER in dispatch (just stores username in ctx.pending_auth_user) and only move PASS out
Defensive: never log passwords; constant-time bcrypt verify always runs even on wrong username.
Acceptance: test_authinfo_correct_password and test_authinfo_wrong_password pass; cargo test clean.
